<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 28,321,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 28,321,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 03/26/97    03/19/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 28,321,000  28,121,000    25,477,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  98,648     131,450	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  35,324,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,516,775	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   03/26/97    03/19/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,999,000   4,921,000     4,156,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,197,000   4,792,000     4,351,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,308,000   4,239,000     4,315,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,931,000   2,876,000     2,767,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,933,000   3,968,000     3,162,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,036,000   5,117,000     4,890,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,918,000   2,207,000     1,836,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	28,321,000  28,121,000    25,477,000</p>
